400 $\mathrm{mV}\cdot\mathbf{s}^{-1}$ indicates that the redox process is surfacecontrolled for NENU-500 and NENU-501-GCE (Figures $\mathbf{S}_{23}$ and $S24$ ).29 In addition, NENU-500 and NENU-501- GCE are highly stable and the peak potentials change little with the increasing scan rates, which is especially useful for electrocatalytic studies. NENU-500 and NENU501-GCE display good electrocatalytic activities in a wide concentration range toward the reduction of ${\mathrm{NO}}_{2}^{-}$ ions (Figures $S25$ and S26). Upon the addition of $\mathsf{N a N O}_{2}$ , the reduction peak currents dramatically increase and the corresponding oxidation peak currents decrease, illustrating that nitrite ion is reduced.30
Furthermore, the HER catalytic activities of assynthesized NENU-499 − NENU-501 were also evaluated by electrochemical experiments. These experiments were carried out in 0.5 M $\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{SO}_{4}$ aqueous solution $\left(\mathrm{pH}=\mathbf{0.16}\right)$ .31 Figure $S_{27}$ described the polarization curve of an NENU500 modified electrode in 0.5 M ${\mathrm{H}}_{2}{\mathrm{SO}}_{4}$ with a scan rate of $5\mathrm{mV^{\cdot}s^{-1}}$ . In order to clarify the factors contributed to the HER performance of NENU-500-RDE (rotating disk electrode), the HER activity of pure XC-72R modified electrode was measured as the reference. As a comparison, NENU-500-doped composites with different contents were also studied. The onset potential for HER of NENU500-doped $\tt X C-72R$ composites modified electrodes is more positive than that of $x{\mathrm{C}}{\mathrm{-}}72{\mathrm{R}}$ modified electrode. Meanwhile, the current density of NENU-500-doped XC72R composites modified electrode is also larger than those of pure NENU-500 or $X C-72R$ electrode when the potential is more negative than 140 mV. That is, the HER activity of NENU-500 modified electrode is obviously enhanced after carbon black doping. These results demonstrate HER activity of POM-based MOF modified electrode is mainly originated from the synergistic effect between POM-based MOF material and carbon black. After careful analysis of these results, we infer that NENU-500 may contribute to the low overpotential and carbon black contributes to the high current density, respectively. It is necessary to dope carbon material into POM-based MOF material, which not only improves the electrical conductivity but also increases the current. The increased content of NENU-500 in composite electrode facilitates charge transfer to some extent and thereby results in improved HER activity. Relatively speaking, the composite with $50\ \mathrm{\wt\%}$ doped amount exhibits better catalytic behavior than that of 20 wt% doping composite. NENU-500 $(50~\mathrm{wt\%})$ shows an onset overpotential of 180 $\mathrm{mV}$ and a Tafel slope of $96\mathrm{mV\cdotdec}^{-1}$ .
Additionally, a series of comparison experiments were also performed under the given conditions. Figure 5a shows the HER polarization curves of various electrocatalysts in 0.5 M $\mathrm{H}_{2}S\mathrm{O}_{4}$ aqueous solution with a scan rate of $5~\mathrm{mV\cdots^{-1}}$ , including NENU-499, NENU-500, and NENU501 modified RDE with loading amount of $50\mathrm{wt\%}$ , as well as bare RDE, pure $x{\mathrm{C}}{-}72{\mathrm{R}}$ and commercial $\mathrm{Pt}/\mathrm{C}$ (20 wt% $\mathrm{Pt/XC-72R)}$ ). Moreover, the HER activities of $\varepsilon(\mathrm{trim})_{4/3},$ NENU- ${\bf\cdot}{\bf5}$ and HKUST-1 were also studied for comparison (Figure S28). As well-known, $\mathrm{Pt}/\mathrm{C}$ exhibits a high activity for HER with nearly zero onset overpotential $(\eta)$ and high current density. Bare RDE shows a very poor HER activity. Pure $X C-72R$ has a negligible electrocatalytic activity, while the doping samples could enhance the HER activity by the introduction of active sites. NENU-500-modified RDE is highly active toward HER and it can approach a large current density of 10 $\mathrm{\mA}{\cdot}\mathrm{cm}^{-2}$ at an overpotential of $237\mathrm{mV}.$ . To compare the required overpotentials for driving a current of 10 $\mathrm{\mA}{\cdot}\mathrm{cm}^{-2}$ $(\eta_{\mathrm{1o}})$ is more practical owing to a solar light-coupled HER apparatus usually runs at $10{-}20\operatorname{mA}{\cdot}\operatorname{cm}^{-2}$ under the standard condition (1 sun, AM 1.5),2 indicating that 10 $\mathrm{\mA}{\cdot}\mathrm{cm}^{-2}$ is meaningful as the point of reference. NENU-501 and $\varepsilon(\mathrm{trim})_{4/3}$ require an overpotential of 392 and $515~\mathrm{mV}$ to achieve a 10 $\mathrm{\mA}{\cdot}\mathrm{cm}^{-2}$ HER current density, respectively. In addition, NENU-499 modified RDE requires an overpotential of $570~\mathrm{mV}.$ , which is larger than those of NENU-500, NENU-501 and $\varepsilon(\mathrm{trim})_{4/3}$ . The $\eta_{\scriptscriptstyle10}$ values were determined to be $585$ and $691~\mathrm{mV}$ for $\mathbf{NENU-5}$ and HKUST-1 modified electrodes (Table 1), respectively, which are even larger than those of other four electrocatalysts. These five catalysts exhibit larger overpotentials than that of NENU-500, suggesting that fast and efficient electron transfer occurs on the NENU-500 modified electrode. The results imply that NENU-500 is much superior in catalytic activity over other five electrodes.
